#doc (Manual) "Path guide" =>

# Path Guide

A project this foundational cannot have one canonical reader. Obsmetrologia needs
routes. A category theorist, Lean formalizer, agent, philosopher, and internal
561 maintainer will ask different first questions.

The path guide records those routes without pretending they are separate
projects.

## First-Time Mathematical Reader

Begin with the program statement, then read marks, utterances, articulating,
predication, positing, and settling. Only after that should recovered category
language or frontier certificates become primary.

The aim is to see the generative order before mapping it onto familiar
mathematics.

## Lean Formalizer

Begin with the dependency policy and primitive declarations. Then read each
manual chapter alongside its corresponding Lean module. Treat examples as
checked prose, not decoration.

The aim is to preserve the free-data boundary. New code should make later
objects from earlier ones rather than smuggling in received assumptions.

## Frontier Agent

Begin with the scope guide and proof status guide. Then place work in a frontier
note before attempting promotion into normative Lean or the foundation manual.

The aim is to let experimental work move quickly while keeping the manual honest.

## Corpus Reader

Begin with concept index entries that connect corpus terms to Obsmetrologia terms.
Then follow the generated mathematical path backwards and forwards.

The aim is to see how the corpus becomes mathematics without flattening the
corpus vocabulary into ordinary textbook language too early.

## Maintainer

Begin with the scope guide, contributor guide, documentation style, and theory
overview template. Use those documents to decide whether a proposed addition
belongs in the manual, generated API docs, blueprint, frontier notes, or archive.
